// **A probe material, not a shipped creature.** One of the two value steps
// `examples/creature_look.rs` measures the findability of a small body
// against -- see `Reports/creature-appearance-design.md`.
//
// The hue is the shipped ant's, to two decimal places on the R:G:B ratio,
// and only the *value* moves. That is deliberate and it is the whole
// design of the experiment: `render.rs`'s gut-tint note records a blind
// A/B in which **hue** lost at one to two cells, and an arm that moved hue
// and value together could not say which one carried the result.
//
// The palette is narrow (14 units end to end) for the reason
// `dead-ends.md` records against `log.ron`: a wide spread makes a field of
// cells draw randomly across a range, which is *speckle*, and speckle
// destroys the one thing a small body has -- its shape.
(
    name: "chitin_mid",
    display: "Chitin (mid)",
    kind: Creature,
    density: 1.0,
    colors: [
        (120, 104, 92),
        (127, 110, 98),
        (113, 98, 87),
    ],
    flammability: 0.6,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 40,
    burns_into: "corpse",
    heat_conductivity: 0.1,
    food_energy: 480.0,
    food_class: 1.0,
)
